# Regenerated from committed sources by `pnpm libdoc` — 8 MB of rendered
# keyword bodies, derived from content/libdoc/*.json.
#
# `app/generated/*` and not `app/generated`: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation below it never matches. The rule read
# `app/generated` and the `!` line under it did nothing — versions.json was
# only in the repository because it had been added before the rule existed.
app/generated/*

# …except the version manifest. nuxt.config.ts reads it while loading the
# config, which happens during `pnpm install`'s prepare step — before any
# script could regenerate it. Ignoring it made a clean clone fail to install.
!app/generated/versions.json

# …and the device descriptors, for the same shape of reason. `pnpm devices`
# downloads playwright-core to read them, so it cannot run during a build:
# `pnpm generate` must work from a clean clone with no network. Ignoring this
# file would leave DeviceRows.server.vue importing something that is not there.
!app/generated/devices.json
